      "name": "Principles of Splinting and Bone Injuries",
      "description": "Splinting: its purpose, when to use it, its principles and sequence, plus the types of bones.",
      "position": 5,
      "updatedAt": 1783971504483,
      "terms": [
        {
          "term": "Splinting",
          "kind": "standard",
          "definition": "Immobilizing an injured body part with rigid or flexible support to prevent movement before medical treatment.",
          "answers": null,
          "position": 0,
          "id": "b4b498f3-d62d-4bdd-acdb-d596f708408c"
        },
        {
          "term": "Splint",
          "kind": "standard",
          "definition": "Device that keeps the injured part stable, reduces pain, and prevents further injury while waiting for medical care.",
          "answers": null,
          "position": 1,
          "id": "cbb9a0ac-1dff-46d3-bd7c-f417c8c76a7d"
        },
        {
